id|kind|question|gold|reference
1|factual|Under Article 5(2), who must be able to show compliance with the data processing principles?|01-EU-GDPR-Regulation-2016-679:36:Article 5 (2)|The controller is responsible for compliance with Article 5(1) and must be able to demonstrate it.
2|factual|Under Article 7(3), does withdrawing consent invalidate processing already carried out on that consent?|01-EU-GDPR-Regulation-2016-679:37:Article 7 (3)|No. Withdrawal does not affect the lawfulness of processing based on consent before withdrawal.
3|factual|How long does Article 12(3) normally give a controller to inform a person about action on a rights request, and when must an extension be communicated?|01-EU-GDPR-Regulation-2016-679:40:Article 12 (3)|Respond without undue delay and within one month of receipt. A necessary extension of up to two more months must be communicated within the initial month with reasons.
4|factual|Under Article 15(3), what may the controller charge for further copies of a person's personal data?|01-EU-GDPR-Regulation-2016-679:43:Article 15 (3)|A reasonable fee based on administrative costs.
5|factual|Under Article 16, what can someone do about incomplete personal data?|01-EU-GDPR-Regulation-2016-679:43:Article 16|Have it completed, taking the processing purposes into account, including by giving a supplementary statement.
6|factual|What risk threshold triggers direct communication to affected people under Article 34(1), and how soon must it happen?|01-EU-GDPR-Regulation-2016-679:52:Article 34 (1)|A breach likely to result in a high risk to people's rights and freedoms. Communicate without undue delay.
7|factual|When is an organisation with fewer than 250 employees still subject to the record-keeping obligations under Article 30(5)?|01-EU-GDPR-Regulation-2016-679:51:Article 30 (5)|When processing is likely to pose a risk to rights and freedoms, is not occasional, or includes special-category or criminal convictions and offences data.
8|factual|Where can a person lodge a GDPR complaint under Article 77(1)?|01-EU-GDPR-Regulation-2016-679:80:Article 77 (1)|With a supervisory authority, in particular in the Member State of habitual residence, work, or the alleged infringement.
9|factual|Under Article 79(2), when is the data subject's home Member State forum unavailable?|01-EU-GDPR-Regulation-2016-679:80:Article 79 (2)|When the controller or processor is a Member State public authority acting in the exercise of its public powers.
10|multi|When must a controller notify the supervisory authority under Article 33(1), and what level of certainty counts as awareness according to the EDPB breach guidelines?|01-EU-GDPR-Regulation-2016-679:52:Article 33 (1);03-EDPB-Breach-Notification:11:*|Without undue delay and where feasible within 72 hours of awareness, unless the breach is unlikely to pose a risk to rights and freedoms. Awareness requires reasonable certainty that a security incident compromised personal data.
11|multi|What does Article 33(2) require a processor to do after discovering a breach, and what does the EDPB recommend if some details are still unavailable?|01-EU-GDPR-Regulation-2016-679:52:Article 33 (2);03-EDPB-Breach-Notification:14:*|Notify the controller without undue delay. The EDPB recommends notifying promptly and sharing further information in phases as details become available.
12|multi|Under Article 7(3), what happens to processing already performed on withdrawn consent, and under Article 15(3), what may be charged for further copies?|01-EU-GDPR-Regulation-2016-679:37:Article 7 (3);01-EU-GDPR-Regulation-2016-679:43:Article 15 (3)|Withdrawal does not affect prior lawful consent-based processing. Further copies may carry a reasonable fee based on administrative costs.
13|unanswerable|On what date did Acme Clinic actually notify its supervisory authority about incident AC-119?||The documents contain no record of that incident.
14|unanswerable|What hourly consulting rate did Northwind agree to pay its external privacy adviser?||The documents contain no consultancy contract or agreed rate.
15|unanswerable|What is the license plate of the vehicle that carried the missing USB drive in the breach example?||The example does not provide a vehicle license plate.
